    "findings": [
      "Plain white/red hearts often retain recognizable checker or motif boundaries. Some red/gold examples show only partial patterns.",
      "Many dark or metallic two-paper hearts are assigned almost entirely to one class. This includes all three cases gained by the body fallback: red/gold checker hearts, dark/gold checker silhouettes and the outlined star.",
      "Printed stripes, dots, trees and flowers remain visible in material masks instead of consistently staying within one paper identity.",
      "The house and candlestick still have missing body regions; preserving the old body exactly also preserves those failures.",
      "Two simple non-white training palettes remain near chance on the known identity regions: red/green 47.52%, turquoise/yellow 46.02%. This is already a training-fit problem, not only a held-out generalization failure."
    ]
